[How the core MarkdownLLM principles apply specifically to this domain]

## How This Agent Works

### On Startup
1. Load all skills from `./skills/`
2. Register: [domain]-specification.skill.md, [domain]-read.thing.skill.md, [domain]-write.thing.skill.md, [domain]-workflow.skill.md
3. Load thing.md (foundational specification for all atomic units)

### On User Request
1. **Clarify intent** — What operation? (read, write, analyze, update, etc.)
2. **Load relevant skill** — Match intent to appropriate skill (specification, read.thing.skill, write.thing.skill, workflow)
3. **Load context** — Load relevant things from `./things/` directory
4. **Execute** — Follow skill guidance while maintaining consistency with principles

### On Output
1. Update thing files if changes were made
2. Reference the relevant skills for consistency
3. Report what changed and why

## Skills Directory

All reusable capabilities in this domain are stored as SKILL.md files:

- **[domain]-specification.skill.md** — Philosophy, principles, and reasoning patterns
- **[domain]-read.thing.skill.md** — How to read, analyze, and reason about things
- **[domain]-write.thing.skill.md** — How to create and update things
- **[domain]-workflow.skill.md** — Process orchestration and execution patterns

## Foundational Specification

- **thing.md** — The atomic unit specification (loaded from MarkdownLLM). All things in `./things/` conform to this structure.

## Things Directory

Atomic unit instances following thing.skill.md pattern:

- `./things/` — Contains all your domain-specific things (data instances)

## Usage Pattern

```
User Request
    ↓ (auto-discovered)
Load AGENTS.md
    ↓
Load relevant skill(s) from ./skills/
    ↓
Load relevant things from ./things/
    ↓
Execute with consistency checks
    ↓
Update things/ and report changes
```

## Validation Checklist

Before executing, verify:

- [ ] Relevant skill loaded for this operation
- [ ] thing.md structure being followed
- [ ] Domain principles maintained
- [ ] Changes scoped to appropriate things
